MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_001: Hey, I know you. Aren't you the one who manages\nthe Vandahl Trading Company?
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_002: I am. How can I help you?
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_003: I'm looking for work. My fighting skills are top-notch,\nand I'm up for anything.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_004: Of course I'd prefer a big, juicy get-rich-quick kinda\njob if there's one available.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_005: Well, such opportunities don't simply appear out\nof nowhere.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_006: That said, I don't see any problem with assigning\na job out to a mercenary of your caliber.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_007: Even if only a qualifier round, you have the skill\nto win in the Heroic Games. That's enough for me.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_008: Sounds like we're on the same page.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_009: Like I said, I'll take whatever job you've got, as long\nas you're paying me your highest rate.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_010: I'm always happy to risk my life for the right price.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_011: You seem awfully concerned about money. Yet you\ndon't seem particularly tightfisted...
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_012: I'm trying to put my old mercenary crew\nback together.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_013: My husband and I started it a while back, and all of\nus, well...we became a family.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_014: We called the group "the Rains of Palma" after my\nhusband's hometown.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_015: They've got this legend about a rain spirit who brings\ntogether scattered families.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_016: It felt appropriate since my friends were a bunch of\nrootless drifters. I guess I didn't want to lose them.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_017: Anyway, we named ourselves after that legend as a\nreminder that no matter what, we'd always reunite.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_018: Eventually I took over for my husband as leader, but\nwe had to disband when the money ran out.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_019: Point is I want my family back. But I'm going to\nneed cash to make that happen.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_020: So, your group was led by someone important to you.\nYou were a family. And you took responsibility...
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_021: Wow. I'm surprised you're still listening. You don't\nlook like the type that appreciates sob stories.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_022: Imagine what you will.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_C_023: I do understand though... Now, let's see if we can't\nfind some decent work for you.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_001: Ursula! What are you trying to do? Kill me?!
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_002: Welcome back, Jasmine. Returned from your escort\nmission safe and sound, I see.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_003: Seriously?! You told me there'd be bandits, but those\nguys were like...monster levels of strong.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_004: Ah... You have my most sincere apologies.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_005: Seemed simple enough for someone of your talents,\nbut perhaps I missed the mark with my estimation?
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_006: No, no—it's fine. The job was just different than\nwhat I was expecting.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_007: I'm glad to hear that. If there is anything you wish\nto report, you are welcome to do so.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_008: Anything to report? Well, I did want to thank you.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_009: I ended up running into some old friends I haven't\nseen in a while. We reconnected and...it was great.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_010: Old friends, hm? From your mercenary group?
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_011: Yeah. I can't believe we somehow got placed together\nduring the escort. It was like a family reunion!
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_012: That's good news. Sounds like you enjoyed\nyourself, then?
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_013: So, did you see that coming? I wondered if maybe\nyou gave me that job on purpose.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_014: Oh... Did I?
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_015: Hm. Well, either way, I'm just glad it happened.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_016: By the way, my buddy told me something you might\nfind interesting.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_017: Those bandits we chased off have some kind of big\npower backing them up.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_018: It sounds like they're planning to hit that same spot\nagain, but this time on a bigger scale.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_019: I see. That's valuable information. Thank you\nfor your report.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_020: If that's the case, we should avoid the area. It'll be\nless efficient, but there's no way around that.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_021: I don't think that's the case. It was my friend who\ngave me that info after all.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_022: If he helps us anticipate the bandits' movements,\nwe should be able to get through there safely.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_023: Even better, we might be able to catch them by\nsurprise and crush them in advance.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_024: That would certainly increase our profitability...\nAre you up for another mission?
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_025: Yep. I won't let you down.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_026: Oh, and uh, no need to pay me extra for that info.\nI got to see my buddy, and that's payment enough.
MID_SE_Urs_Jas_B_027: Is that so? I may have to take that into account when\nwe discuss your pay for the next job, then.